To create a draggable `div` that pulls back to its original position after being dragged, you can use JavaScript along with CSS for styling. This can be achieved using vanilla JavaScript or libraries like jQuery UI or Draggable.js. Below, I'll show you how to do this using plain JavaScript.

### HTML Structure

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Draggable Div</title>
    <style>
        #draggable {
            width: 100px;
            height: 100px;
            background-color: lightblue;
            position: absolute;
            cursor: move;
            z-index: 1000; /* Ensure it's on top of other elements */
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

<div id="draggable">Drag me!</div>

<script src="script.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

### JavaScript Logic

Create a file named `script.js` and add the following code:

```javascript
document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', (event) => {
    const draggable = document.getElementById('draggable');

    let isDragging = false;
    let offset = { x: 0, y: 0 };

    draggable.addEventListener('mousedown', (e) => {
        isDragging = true;
        offset.x = e.clientX - draggable.offsetLeft;
        offset.y = e.clientY - draggable.offsetTop;
    });

    document.addEventListener('mousemove', (e) => {
        if (isDragging) {
            draggable.style.left = `${e.clientX - offset.x}px`;
            draggable.style.top = `${e.clientY - offset.y}px`;
        }
    });

    document.addEventListener('mouseup', () => {
        isDragging = false;

        // Calculate new position relative to the original one
        const originalPosition = { x: draggable.offsetLeft, y: draggable.offsetTop };
        const newOffsetX = e.clientX - originalPosition.x;
        const newOffsetY = e.clientY - originalPosition.y;

        // Bring the div back to the original position
        draggable.style.left = originalPosition.x + 'px';
        draggable.style.top = originalPosition.y + 'px';

        setTimeout(() => {
            draggable.style.transition = 'left 0s, top 0s'; // Remove transition to ensure immediate update
            draggable.style.left = originalPosition.x + newOffsetX + 'px';
            draggable.style.top = originalPosition.y + newOffsetY + 'px';
            draggable.style.transition = 'left 0.3s, top 0.3s'; // Add transition for smooth movement
        }, 0); // Ensure the next frame
    });
});
```

